// `clock()` in the AOT backend (BACKLOG §6 item 25).
//
// The chunk captures a monotonic counter at entry into the hidden `$clockOrigin`
// global and `clock()` subtracts it, so what it reports is elapsed time rather
// than an absolute counter. Only the *shape* is asserted, never a value: the VM
// and the binary run at different times.
//
// Every target backs this one -- the origin comes from `clock_gettime`, libc,
// `GetTickCount64` or the bare-metal PIT counter -- so the fixture carries no
// `args()`: that builtin is Linux-only and lives in `native_build_args.oskl`.

var a = clock();
print("clock type", type(a));
print("clock non-negative", a >= 0.0);
// `inf >= 0.0` and `inf >= inf` are both true, so the two assertions above
// accepted a broken conversion. Elapsed time is small, so bound it: an
// implementation that divides by a denormal overflows to +inf and fails here.
print("clock finite", a < 1000000000.0);
var b = clock();
print("clock monotonic", b >= a);
var c = clock();
print("clock elapsed finite", c - a < 1000000000.0);
